cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "TB-BOPAS: a Bayesian priority-action score applied to India's drug-resistant tuberculosis surveillance, 2017-2024"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, input data and outputs for a study applying a Bayesian
  priority-action score to India's drug-resistant tuberculosis surveillance.
  Five national axes were reconstructed from WHO Global TB Programme country
  data with per-datapoint provenance. No axis is significantly worsening;
  treatment success improved by +4.23 (MDR/RR-TB) and +6.38 (XDR-TB) percentage
  points per year. Fitting across an uncorrected 2021 reporting discontinuity is
  by itself sufficient to manufacture a confident top-ranked priority on an axis
  that is in fact improving.
type: dataset
